# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# A PD
# attempting an ungranted access faults. Each fault must be caught by the
# parent PD and reported, and the bystander PD must answer after each one.
#
# The order follows from the priorities in isolation-test.system (one core).
# Fault lines name what was accessed and why it failed, not code addresses
# or translation levels, so they do not change from build to build; the
# "fault detail" lines that follow them carry those and are not checked.
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: starting; children probe_unmapped (0) and probe_readonly (1)
NOWAYOS: isolation-bystander: starting; private page at 0x40000000 holds 0x5afec0de
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: probe_unmapped reading 0x40000000, which is not mapped in this PD
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: probe_unmapped stopped: data read at 0x40000000: translation fault (nothing mapped there)
NOWAYOS: isolation-bystander: still running (check 1); private page intact
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: bystander answered after fault 1
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: probe_readonly read 0x00000000 from its read-only page at 0x50000000
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: probe_readonly writing to its read-only page at 0x50000000
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: probe_readonly stopped: data write at 0x50000000: permission fault (the mapping does not allow it)
NOWAYOS: isolation-bystander: still running (check 2); private page intact
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: bystander answered after fault 2
NOWAYOS: isolation-test: 2 of 2 forbidden accesses faulted and were contained; bystander still running

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a forbidden access that succeeded, a fault the monitor had to handle (a PD
# other than a probe faulted), a kernel error message (such as a fault reply
# left pending), a panic, or anything unexpected.
!ISOLATION FAILURE
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!CHANGED
!cannot
!unexpected
!NOT stopped
!no probe is defined
